  #line-at(46.8pt, 448.39pt, "The δ-doped epitaxial structure (Figure 1(a)) used in this work ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 459.91pt, "was grown by MOCVD in an Agnitron Agilis 100 system. ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 471.43pt, "First, ~50 nm of UID β-Ga₂O₃ was grown at 600°C, 15 Torr ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 482.95pt, "using Ar carrier gas and Triethylgallium (TEGa) and O")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 3.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(284.09pt, 483.43pt, "2")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(286.01pt, 482.95pt, " as ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 494.47pt, "precursors to trap the residual Fe tail [19] followed by a ~300 ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 505.87pt, "nm UID buffer. For the δ-doped layer, the sample was dosed ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 517.39pt, "with ~20 nmol of silane post a TEGa purge followed by a final ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 528.91pt, "cap layer of ~30 nm of UID β-Ga₂O₃. An ohmic contact ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 540.43pt, "regrowth process was used to achieve low contact resistance. ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 551.95pt, "The source and drain regions were first patterned with a thick ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 563.35pt, "PECVD grown SiO")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 3.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(127.82pt, 563.83pt, "2")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(129.86pt, 563.35pt, " hard mask. Post patterning, the β-Ga₂O₃ ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 574.9pt, "epilayer was etched to a depth of 60 nm and regrown with ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 586.42pt, "heavily doped n-type β-Ga₂O₃ with doping concentration of 1 ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 597.94pt, "× 10")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 3.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(65.304pt, 595.9pt, "20")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(69.384pt, 597.94pt, " cm")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 3.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(84.384pt, 595.9pt, "−3")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(88.584pt, 597.94pt, " to achieve low contact resistance [6]. Fin structures ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 609.46pt, "(100 nm width (W")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 3.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(121.82pt, 609.94pt, "f")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(123.14pt, 609.46pt, "), 200 nm spacing (W")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 3.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(211.25pt, 609.94pt, "s")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(212.81pt, 609.46pt, ")) were defined using ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 620.98pt, "e-beam lithography and then etched to 100 nm depth using a ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 632.38pt, "low power BCl")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 3.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(109.7pt, 632.86pt, "3")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(111.74pt, 632.38pt, " based ICP-RIE process to minimize sidewall ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 643.9pt, "etch damage to the δ-doped channel. A bilayer composite ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 655.42pt, "mask consisting of 10 nm SiO")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 3.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(175.94pt, 655.9pt, "2 ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(180.65pt, 655.42pt, "and ZEP 520A ebeam resist ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 666.94pt, "was used to carry out the fin etch process. After defining the ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 678.46pt, "fins, 200 nm mesa etch was performed for device isolation. To ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 689.98pt, "reduce gate leakage, 7 nm thick Al")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 3.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(204.77pt, 690.46pt, "2")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(206.81pt, 689.98pt, "O")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 3.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(214.01pt, 690.46pt, "3")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(216.05pt, 689.98pt, " was deposited via ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 701.376pt, "plasma assisted ALD as the gate dielectric. The Al₂O₃ over the ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 712.896pt, "ohmic regions was selectively removed using BCl₃ etching for ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 724.416pt, "source/drain metallization. A Ti/Au (40nm/60nm) stack was ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 735.96pt, "then deposited via e-beam evaporation followed by short RTA ")
  #line-at(313.27pt, 59.76pt, "anneal (470°C, 1 min, N₂ ambient) to form the ohmic contacts. ")
  #line-at(313.27pt, 71.28pt, "Finally, a 100 nm Schottky Ni gate was deposited using e-")
  #line-at(313.27pt, 82.7pt, "beam evaporation with 180-degree sample rotation for even ")
  #line-at(313.27pt, 94.22pt, "deposition on the gate sidewall. The fabricated device is ")
  #line-at(313.27pt, 105.74pt, "imaged using scanning electron microscope and shown in ")
  #line-at(313.27pt, 117.26pt, "Figure 1(b) and 1(c).")
  #set text(font: "Arial", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
